# LAB ACTION PLAN – WEEK 6 Docker Compose

## Navigate to Project Folder
```
mkdir ~/compose-lab
cd ~/compose-lab
```

## Create docker-compose.yml (Initial Setup)
```
version: "3.9"
services:
  web:
    image: nginx:latest
    ports:
      - "8080:80"
  db:
    image: postgres:15
    environment:
      POSTGRES_USER: demo
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: demo
      POSTGRES_DB: demo_db
```

## Run Multi-Container Setup
```
docker compose up -d
```

## Open Browser to Verify Nginx
```
http://localhost:8080
```

## Modify docker-compose.yml to Add Redis
```
services:
  redis:
    image: redis:alpine
  web:
    image: nginx:latest
    ports:
      - "8080:80"
    depends_on:
      - redis
```

## Restart Services
```
docker compose up -d
docker compose ps
```

## Zip and Transfer Folder (Deploy to Another Machine)
```
zip -r compose-lab.zip compose-lab
# Transfer zip to new machine
docker compose up -d
```

## Add Custom Network and Volume
```
networks:
  app-net:

volumes:
  db-data:

services:
  web:
    image: nginx:latest
    ports:
      - "8080:80"
    networks:
      - app-net
    depends_on:
      - db
  db:
    image: postgres:15
    environment:
      POSTGRES_USER: demo
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: demo
      POSTGRES_DB: demo_db
    volumes:
      - db-data:/var/lib/postgresql/data
    networks:
      - app-net
```

## Run with Network and Volume
```
docker compose up -d
```

## Stop Containers
```
docker compose down
```

## Start Again
```
docker compose up -d
```

## Create Simple Flask App (app.py)
```
from flask import Flask
app = Flask(__name__)
@app.route("/")
def home():
    return "Hello from Flask + Docker!"
if __name__ == "__main__":
    app.run(host="0.0.0.0", port=5000)
```

## Create Dockerfile for Flask App
```
FROM python:3.10-slim
WORKDIR /app
COPY app.py /app/
RUN pip install flask
CMD ["python", "app.py"]
```

## Update docker-compose.yml for Flask App
```
services:
  web:
    build: .
    ports:
      - "5000:5000"
    depends_on:
      - db
```

## Build and Run Flask App
```
docker compose up --build
```

## Rebuild After Changes
```
docker compose up --build
```

